## Test behavior through meaningful dependency seams
Keep the behavior under test real. For deterministic tests, stub a narrow external effect (network, clock, filesystem, process) instead of the whole module under test. Use existing seams; do not add an interface for every helper. Module mocks are allowed when a narrower supported seam is unavailable and real behavior still runs.
```python
# bad: no production behavior runs
monkeypatch.setattr(billing, "load_balance", lambda account: 25)
assert billing.load_balance("demo") == 25
```
```python
# good: production parsing runs; only its network effect is replaced
monkeypatch.setattr(billing.transport, "get", lambda path: {"balance": 25})
assert billing.load_balance("demo") == 25
```
