## Verify external command names before mirroring them in fixtures
A passing fake CLI does not prove that the installed tool accepts its resource names or options. Verify new command vocabulary through installed discovery/help or an actual read-only call, then make fixtures reject unsupported inputs. Existing call syntax copied from the implementation is not independent evidence.
```python
# bad: the fake accepts this invented plural, so the test passes
subprocess.run(["kubectl", "get", "pvcs", "-A", "-o", "json"], check=True)
```
```python
# good: canonical resource verified against the installed API
subprocess.run(["kubectl", "get", "persistentvolumeclaims", "-A", "-o", "json"], check=True)
```
Verified tool shortcuts remain valid. Test unavailable collection separately from successful empty output, and prove the real read path before declaring integration complete.
