## Validate with the project-pinned tool version
A clean newer local linter does not prove the pinned CI linter accepts the same source. Check the actual version and use the project pin for the final gate; default checks and parsing can differ between releases.
```python
# bad: CI pins another version, but this unspecified local binary is the proof
subprocess.run(["ruff", "check", *paths], check=True)
```
```python
# good: this environment was provisioned with the verified CI version
subprocess.run([str(ci_venv / "bin" / "ruff"), "check", *paths], check=True)
```
An existing container or environment with the verified pin is equally valid; no new environment is required when the installed tool already matches.
