Generated test helpers must use an interpreter present in the target test environment. A Python image can provide Python under /usr/local/bin without /usr/bin/python3.
```python
# bad: the helper executes only on hosts with this particular path
helper.write_text("#!/usr/bin/python3\n" + body)
```
```python
# good: the helper uses the same interpreter that is running the test
helper.write_text(f"#!{sys.executable}\n" + body)
```
Exercise the helper in the actual CI image when path or runtime parity matters; a local green run alone cannot establish that parity.
