## Exercise the intended validation boundary
A corrupted outer receipt can reject a negative fixture before its intended
semantic guard runs. Rebind synthetic enclosing digests after mutation and
assert the intended rejection at the actual entry point. Keep such receipts
strictly test-only. For paginated APIs test source, page order, and terminal
evidence according to the specific API contract; do not infer completeness
from a plausible item count.
```python
# bad: stale enclosing digest can fail before the source policy is checked
mutated = change_source(fixture, "web")
with pytest.raises(ValueError):
    validate(mutated, original_receipt)
```
```python
# good: this synthetic receipt reaches and names the semantic guard
mutated = change_source(fixture, "web")
receipt = build_synthetic_receipt_for(mutated)
with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="pipeline source"):
    validate(mutated, receipt)
```
```python
# bad: expected count alone does not establish a terminal page
assert len(jobs) == expected_count
```
```python
# good: validate actual page metadata and terminal response too
assert_pipeline_source(pipeline, expected="push")
assert_complete_ordered_pages(page_receipts, expected_terminal=[])
assert len(jobs) == expected_count
```
